s://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107238.patch","merged_at":"2025-06-09T22:12:39Z"},"body":"At the moment, if you make a shader that uses both `shadow_to_opacity` and `unshaded` when using the Compatibility renderer, it will fail to compile with the following error:\r\n\r\n```\r\nE 0:00:02:007   _display_error_with_code: SceneShaderGLES3: Fragment shader compilation failed:\r\nERROR: 0:1817: 'ambient_light' : undeclared identifier\r\nERROR: 1 compilation errors.  No code generated.\r\n  <C++ Source>  drivers/gles3/shader_gles3.cpp:259 @ _display_error_with_code()\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis PR fixes that!\r\n\r\nThis problem doesn't happen with the Forward+ or Mobile renderers, where the result is full transparency (`alpha = 0.0`), even though the scene shaders in those renders don't set it explicitly, like in this PR. I don't know if it'd be worth changing Forward+ and Mobile to do it explicitly too?","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107238/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0